{"title":"Canada Lynx Mathematical Competition","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The CLMC, or Canada Lynx Mathematical Competition, is a national math contest by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Canadian_Mathematical_Society&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Canadian Mathematical Society (page does not exist)\">Canadian Mathematical Society</a> (CMS) for students in grades K-12 (especially 7-12), designed to build confidence and interest in math by presenting it as fun, featuring 15 multiple-choice questions from the core curriculum, and offering feedback and prizes. It serves as a great entry point and warm-up for the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Canadian_Open_Mathematics_Challenge\" title=\"Canadian Open Mathematics Challenge\">Canadian Open Mathematics Challenge</a> (COMC) and is held annually around October at schools with a teacher proctor.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Canada_Lynx_Mathematical_Competition&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CLMC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"CLMC Problems and Solutions\">CLMC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Canada_Lynx_Mathematical_Competition&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018075246\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.018 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 11/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 349/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0